## Problem

Token group renaming had significant performance issues:

1. **Detection phase lag**: Selecting "Yes" to rename caused noticeable delay before the modal appeared due to expensive O(n×m×k) nested loops checking which token sets contain the tokens being renamed
2. **Execution bottleneck**: Slow renaming execution caused by individual `renameTokenAcrossSets` calls with redundant token set searches for each token

## Solution

**Removed detection overhead**: Always show "Rename in other sets" option for token groups without pre-checking, eliminating the expensive nested loops that caused modal delay.

**Optimized execution**: Replaced individual token processing with a single efficient scan through token sets followed by batch operations.

## Technical Details

### Before (Performance Issues)
```typescript
// Expensive O(n*m*k) detection before showing modal
const tokenSetsContainingSameTokens: string[] = [];
tokensToRename.forEach((tokenToRename) => {
  Object.entries(tokens).forEach(([tokenSet, tokenList]) => {
    if (tokenSet !== activeTokenSet && tokenList.find((token) => token.name === tokenToRename.oldName)) {
      // Nested loops causing lag
    }
  });
});

// Individual calls with redundant searches during execution
await Promise.all(
  tokensToRename.map(async (tokenToRename) => {
    // Another search through all token sets for each token
    const setsContainingToken: string[] = [activeTokenSet];
    Object.entries(tokens).forEach(([tokenSet, tokenList]) => {
      // Redundant work
    });
  })
);
```

### After (Optimized)
```typescript
// Always show option - no detection overhead
choices.push({
  key: ModalOptions.RENAME_ACROSS_SETS,
  label: 'Rename in other sets',
});

// Single efficient scan + batch processing
const relevantTokenSets = new Set<string>();
Object.entries(tokens).forEach(([tokenSet, tokenList]) => {
  const hasRelevantToken = tokensToRename.some((tokenToRename) =>
    tokenList.some((token) => token.name === tokenToRename.oldName)
  );
  if (hasRelevantToken) relevantTokenSets.add(tokenSet);
});

// Batch process with pre-computed token sets
await Promise.all(
  tokensToRename.map((tokenToRename) =>
    dispatch.tokenState.renameTokenAcrossSets({
      oldName: tokenToRename.oldName,
      newName: tokenToRename.newName,
      type,
      tokenSets: Array.from(relevantTokenSets),
    })
  )
);
```

## Results

- ✅ **Instant modal display**: No lag when selecting "Yes" to rename
- ✅ **Fast execution**: Significantly faster renaming with minimal redundant operations  
- ✅ **Consistent UX**: Users always see cross-set option for groups (matches individual token behavior)
- ✅ **No breaking changes**: Existing functionality preserved, purely performance optimization

## Testing

- ✅ Build passes (development and production)
- ✅ Linting passes  
- ✅ All useTokens tests continue to pass
- ✅ No regressions in existing functionality

